    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) represent our strongest offensive engines. **Lawrence Butler** benefits immensely from a favorable encounter with Javier (5.16 xERA), where his elite matchup profile and platoon advantage override a slightly neutral park factor. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** is positioned for a high-ceiling performance; his 16% park boost combined with a strong platoon edge against Baz makes him a primary target for counting stats. While **Bryce Harper** (64.81) and **JJ Bleday** (66.17) provide solid, reliable production, the overall projected efficiency of our lineup is driven by these specific platoon-matchup synergies that capitalize on sub-5.00 xERA starters.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision involved **Jung Hoo Lee** (48.89), who hovered right at the threshold but ultimately yielded to the higher floor provided by our current outfield depth. While **Jung Hoo Lee** offers high-speed upside, his negative dynamic platoon split against the lefty Bennett capped his efficiency, making him a less attractive option compared to the surging **Dylan Beavers**, whose massive 17% SP skill boost against Martinez creates a more favorable Roto profile today. We are also keeping a close watch on **Cal Raleigh** (56.88); while his power profile is potent, he faces the toughest matchup of our starters against Imanaga (3.69 xERA). If any further lineup adjustments or weather alerts emerge regarding the late games, we will look to rotate in **Daulton Varsho** or **Braden Montgomery** if their relative platoon environment improves, but for now, the current configuration offers the most robust path toward maximizing our Roto gains.",
